From 2769f991ce6680e201652e10aa8c97ca4619d076 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MikolajQ <mikolaj.q@wp.pl>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:05:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DefaultDeviceEffectsApplier: Add Wi-Fi and Bluetooth effects

Airplane mode is not a reliable way to turn Wi-Fi and Bluetooth off for
the night: with the airplane mode enhancement, Android remembers whether
the user last kept each of them on in airplane mode, so a bedtime mode
with minimizeRadioUsage may leave Wi-Fi on one night and off the next.

Add "disable Wi-Fi" and "disable Bluetooth" extra effects, with or
without airplane mode. Like the airplane mode and location effects they
only undo what the mode did, persist that across reboots, and leave a
radio the user turned back on alone.

The order matters: a radio toggled while airplane mode is on becomes
the user's airplane mode preference. So Wi-Fi and Bluetooth are turned
off before airplane mode turns on, and back on only after airplane mode
is off, with a short delay (holding a wake lock) as both services see
the airplane mode change asynchronously. All radio changes, airplane
mode included, now wait together for an ongoing call to end, as turning
Wi-Fi or Bluetooth off could drop a Wi-Fi call or move its audio away
from a headset. Effects applied while booting wait for the boot to
complete before touching Wi-Fi or Bluetooth.

Assisted-by: LLM
